.TH tkcanvaspng n 0.2 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkcanvaspng
.PP
Render a Tk \fBcanvas\fR to a \fBPNG\fR (pure Tcl, no external tools) via \fBtclutils::tupngdraw\fR. Useful for exporting canvas drawings/charts. Requires Tk plus \fBtclutils::tupngdraw\fR; TTF text needs the optional \fBGlyphs\fR package. Optional widget (not in the tkutils umbrella).
.SS API
.CS
package require tkutils::tkcanvaspng

# PNG bytes of the canvas:
set png [::tkutils::tkcanvaspng::render $canvas \
    ?-region {x1 y1 x2 y2}? ?-scale N? ?-background color? \
    ?-textcmd cmd? ?-fontmap map?]

# write straight to a file (returns the file name):
::tkutils::tkcanvaspng::write out.png $canvas ?same options?
.CE
.IP \(bu
\fB\-region\fR defaults to \fB[$canvas bbox all]\fR; an empty canvas is an error.
.IP \(bu
\fB\-scale\fR is a positive\-integer pixel multiplier.
.IP \(bu
\fB\-background\fR defaults to the canvas background, else white.
.IP \(bu
\fB\-fontmap\fR maps Tk fonts to TTF files for glyph rendering (needs \fBGlyphs\fR).
.SS Errors
.PP
\fB{TKUTILS TKCANVASPNG <REASON>}\fR (\fBWINDOW\fR, \fBEMPTY\fR).
.SS "See also"
.PP
\fBtclutils::tupngdraw\fR, \fBtclutils::tupng\fR.
